        {
          "id": 520771495,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It is supposed to be a 16 bit field, according to the spec. The entire family of specs is annoying because ANSI/ISO/IEC wants to charge for the ISO/IEC 13818-6 (and -1, and the rest.) However, various specs that refer to implementations are free, whether through ETSI for [DVB](https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_en/301100_301199/301192/01.06.01_20/en_301192v010601a.pdf) or through the [English translation of the Japanese implementation of the standard by ARIB](https://www.arib.or.jp/english/std_tr/broadcasting/std-b24.html), which is free to download (but they make people pay for the Japanese version.) Anyway, you can find in there that in a DII message: \"**privateDataLength**: This 16-bit field indicates the byte length of the following PrivateDataByte field.\"",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
